      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. i'm looking at them now. \n\nto be honest, these feel a bit... unnatural? like, i don't think a real person would ever actually ask \"how did you foster a truly innovative solution to achieve shared growth-mindset goals\" in a real interview. it sounds like you're just trying to hit all those keywords i listed.\n\ncan you try again? i really need these to sound like something a human recruiter would actually say. try to keep the questions professional but conversational, and please—really focus on the quality of the question rather than trying to force those specific words into the text. i'd rather have a lower \"theme score\" than questions that sound like a word salad.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
